    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Children may benefit from nucleoside or nucleotide analog, used only w a pediatric hepatologist. AASLD 9A: antiviral tx in HBeAg+ children (2 to < 18 y) w both ↑ ALT and measurable HBV DNA (goal: HBeAg seroconversion); 9B: ⍉ antivirals in HBeAg+ children w persistently norm ALT, regardless of HBV DNA. Entecavir = approved for children ≥ 2 y. Tenofovir alafenamide (Vemlidy): ≥ 6 y and ≥ 25 kg w compensated liver dz."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Entecavir = first-line (↑potency; resistance uncommon)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tenofovir = the most potent PO HBV antiviral; minimal resistance."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Preg, HBsAg+ w HBV DNA >200,000 IU/mL: tenofovir from 28 wks until delivery."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
